 Delete /admin/delete?username=carlos
```

---

# Key Takeaways

- PHP serialization is not inherently insecure.
- The vulnerability arises when applications trust serialized data supplied by the client.
- Loose type comparisons (`==`) can introduce Type Juggling vulnerabilities.
- Authentication and authorization data should never be stored in unsigned client-side serialized objects.
- Session integrity should always be protected using server-side storage or cryptographic signatures.
